    "Actual results for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2023, as the city reported them to the Census Bureau's Annual Survey of State and Local Government Finances. Not a budget.",
    "The Census surveys every government only in Census of Governments years (2022) and a sample in other years, so FY 2023 is the latest available.",
    "Public schools are run by separate school districts, so they are not included. Residents also pay Garfield County.",
    "Covers every fund, including water, sewer, electric and other utilities. Debt service counts interest and principal repaid; borrowing and transfers between funds are left out.",
    "The city borrowed $8,000 during the year, which is not counted as revenue but helps explain spending above revenue.",
    "Payments to other governments ($1,000) are left out, because the government receiving them reports that spending.",
    "Courts, legal services, public buildings, housing and community development count as overhead.",
    "Debt is long-term debt outstanding plus short-term debt at year end.",
    "Political money is not scored: no candidates for mayor and council of City of Pomeroy reported business, union or PAC contributions to the Public Disclosure Commission since 2023.",
